 "background_floor": 0.055937,
 "finding": "Telling one layout from another is bounded as detection is, and depth ambiguity does not rescue a reader: the same-depth bound holds for every allowed vertical transformation. Under Giza's regional microseism level the oracle, told everything but which layout is there, tells an L-shaped from a straight tunnel with detection minus false alarm at most 1.5e-06, and a column with a spiral from a plain column at most 2.0e-06; the tight bound gives 1.0e-09 and 1.3e-09; the loose certificate with the background caps discrimination at 5.024% at 5% for every pair. Discrimination needs 1.2 to 4.1 times the signal that detecting the first layout needs. With a lorry bouncing beside the layouts all pass, known exactly, the hardest-to-exclude pair (L_tunnel vs branching_tunnel) gives the oracle 0.81 at 70 Hz, 1.2 times short of 95% at 5%: the open regime for shape as for detection. Only these layouts, this rock and these sources are covered."
}